A weathered wooden treasure chest sits half-open in a misty forest clearing, with multiple translucent protective shells nested around it like layers of an onion, each shell glowing with a different subtle color—amber, teal, silver. Delicate golden chains with intricate locks connect the shells together. From the chest, faint wisps of luminescent vapor escape upward, transforming into abstract geometric patterns that dissolve into the fog. The forest floor is covered in fallen leaves and moss, with ancient tree roots creating natural barriers around the chest. Soft, diffused sunlight filters through the canopy above, creating god rays that illuminate the protective layers. The atmosphere is mysterious yet serene, suggesting hidden treasures carefully guarded by multiple enchanted barriers. Studio Ghibli style with rich, painterly textures, soft color gradients, and that distinctive hand-drawn warmth with meticulous attention to natural details and magical elements coexisting harmoniously.
